// Canasta — Classic Canasta, 4 players in teams.
//
// Rules source: https://www.pagat.com/rummy/canasta.html (fetched live per
// CLAUDE.md). Two 52-card packs plus four jokers (108 cards); partners sit
// across; eleven cards each; play clockwise from dealer's left. Each turn:
// draw the top of the stock OR take the WHOLE discard pile (only ever legal
// when its top card can immediately feed a meld of that rank), meld as
// desired, then discard one card. Melds are 3+ cards of one rank with at
// least two naturals and at most three wilds (jokers and deuces are wild); a
// side keeps one meld per rank, growing across turns under either partner's
// adds; seven or more cards make a canasta (natural 500 / mixed 300). The
// discard pile is FROZEN by any wild discard (and by a wild/red-three
// turn-up at the deal), and is always frozen against a side that has not yet
// melded: a frozen pile is taken only with two natural cards of the top rank
// from hand. Unfrozen, the top card may also meld with one natural + one
// wild, or join the side's standing meld. Black threes block the pile while
// on top and meld only as a going-out group; red threes are bonus cards,
// laid out and replaced on sight. A side's first meld must meet the minimum
// count (15/50/90/120 by cumulative score; taking the pile counts only the
// top card toward it). Going out — shedding every card, with or without a
// final discard — requires the side to own a canasta and pays 100. When the
// stock runs out play continues on forced/voluntary pile takes until a
// player entitled to draw cannot; then the hand scores: melded card points
// plus canasta and red-three bonuses, minus card points left in hands.
//
// Simplifications (explicit, per corpus policy — everything else is the
// Pagat classic game):
//   - a fixed FOUR-deal match replaces "first side to 5000" (the
//     initial-meld minimum still reads the real cumulative-score brackets,
//     including the negative-score 15);
//   - the initial meld minimum must be met by a SINGLE meld (plus the pile's
//     top card when taking); the real game may combine several melds laid in
//     the same turn;
//   - the optional "may I go out?" partner question and the concealed-hand
//     double bonus are omitted;
//   - the first dealer is seat 0; the deal rotates left each hand.
//
// Encoding notes (decision structure, not rule changes):
//   - Melding is announce-then-stage: `start_meld(rank)` (or a pile take)
//     opens an attempt, cards join it one at a time through the public
//     `stage` zone, and `close_meld` commits the pile — each stage/close
//     guarded by the canasta.py completability core so every reachable
//     staging state still closes legally (Gin's arrange-guard totality,
//     per card). No `where jointly` selection: canasta108 holds duplicate
//     identical cards, which the combo block's frozenset canonicalization
//     cannot tell apart (guarded loudly at ActionSpace.for_game).
//   - The per-(side, rank) melds are eleven team-indexed zone families plus
//     the black-three go-out pile — the zone-family flattening of
//     decisions.md "Meld groups: flattened zone families".
//   - `pile_frozen` stays a boolean: no rule's `applies_when:` reads it —
//     it gates only take-pile preconditions (decisions.md "The
//     boolean-as-sub-phase criterion", which zone state does not change).
//   - Black threes never freeze the pile; they block it purely by SITTING
//     on top (no take reaches a non-natural top card), so no extra state.
//   - The `ranking:` is deliberately PARTIAL — exactly the eleven meldable
//     natural ranks — so the Rank move-parameter domain of start_meld /
//     add_to_meld is the meldable set by construction (threes, deuces and
//     jokers are never a meld's rank).

game Canasta {

  players: 4
  teams: [[0, 2], [1, 3]]   // partners sit across
  direction: clockwise
  // Measured over seeded random playouts (tests/test_playout_canasta.py):
  // the longest of seeds 0..29 makes 1224 decisions across the four deals.
  // Raise only with a measurement.
  max_length: 8000

  cards: canasta108
  // The meldable natural ranks, strongest first — a deliberately partial
  // ranking: it is the Rank iteration/parameter domain (threes and the wild
  // ranks are excluded by construction). Canasta has no trick ranking.
  ranking: A K Q J 10 9 8 7 6 5 4
  // Card points: jokers 50, deuces and aces 20, K..8 ten, 7..4 and threes 5.
  // Rank-keyed like every card fact: the "3" row is what a black three counts
  // (red threes are bonus objects, swept out of hands on sight, so the row
  // never prices one in play).
  card_points {
    Joker: 50  2: 20  A: 20
    K: 10  Q: 10  J: 10  10: 10  9: 10  8: 10
    7: 5  6: 5  5: 5  4: 5  3: 5
  }

  // What this game borrows from outside the DSL at a CALL position,
  // implemented in `cardlang/runtime/canasta.py`: the pile-take guards, the
  // meld-window guards, and the per-pile canasta bonus. Each entry declares
  // what its own implementation consults, so the clauses differ — only a take
  // guard reads the pile's take-able top, only a window guard reads the open
  // attempt's stage zone and the state that names it, and the bonus reads
  // nothing but the meld piles it prices.
  //
  // The grain is the read an entry can REACH, not the module's union: a
  // helper branch a caller closes with a literal is not that caller's read.
  // `canasta_can_start` announces from hand and never takes, so the pile's
  // buried remainder is beyond it; the initial-meld minimum, by contrast,
  // turns on live state, so every entry that can price one reads `score`.
  //
  // `meld_rank`, `pile_frozen`, `taking_pile` and `team_melded` are declared
  // by `phase hand`, not by the game, so a read of one names that phase —
  // and the phase named `hand` is not the zone family `hand`, which the
  // read's own position tells apart. The tail rides the READ, not the
  // clause: `score` and every zone are game-level and carry none. Naming the
  // phase also promises what the resolver then checks — an entry reading
  // `in hand` is called only where that phase is running, which here is its
  // descendant `phase play`: that phase's own body, and the move types it
  // alone offers.
  //
  // A binder narrows a read to the instance the call names: a player-keyed
  // entry sees that player's hand, and in the meld window that player's
  // stage; the bonus sees its own side's piles. The side a player-keyed entry
  // reasons about is derived from the seating, which no parameter binds, so
  // its meld and `team_melded` reads stay whole.
  primitives {
    canasta_can_take_pile(p : Player) : Boolean
        reads hand[p], pile_top, pile_rest,
              meldA, meldK, meldQ, meldJ, meld10, meld9,
              meld8, meld7, meld6, meld5, meld4, meld3b, score,
              pile_frozen in hand, team_melded in hand
    canasta_must_take_pile(p : Player) : Boolean
        reads hand[p], pile_top, pile_rest,
              meldA, meldK, meldQ, meldJ, meld10, meld9,
              meld8, meld7, meld6, meld5, meld4, meld3b, score,
              pile_frozen in hand, team_melded in hand
    canasta_can_start(p : Player, rank : Rank) : Boolean
        reads hand[p],
              meldA, meldK, meldQ, meldJ, meld10, meld9,
              meld8, meld7, meld6, meld5, meld4, meld3b, score,
              pile_frozen in hand, team_melded in hand
    canasta_stage_ok(p : Player, card : Card) : Boolean
        reads hand[p], stage[p], pile_rest,
              meldA, meldK, meldQ, meldJ, meld10, meld9,
              meld8, meld7, meld6, meld5, meld4, meld3b, score,
              meld_rank in hand, pile_frozen in hand,
              taking_pile in hand, team_melded in hand
    canasta_close_ok(p : Player) : Boolean
        reads hand[p], stage[p], pile_rest,
              meldA, meldK, meldQ, meldJ, meld10, meld9,
              meld8, meld7, meld6, meld5, meld4, meld3b, score,
              meld_rank in hand, pile_frozen in hand,
              taking_pile in hand, team_melded in hand
    canasta_canasta_bonus(u : Team) : Integer
        reads meldA[u], meldK[u], meldQ[u], meldJ[u],
              meld10[u], meld9[u], meld8[u], meld7[u],
              meld6[u], meld5[u], meld4[u], meld3b[u]
  }

  zones {
    deck           : Deck                  // the face-down stock
    hand[player]   : Hand<player>
    stage[player]  : PlayerPile<player>    // the open meld attempt (public, as at a table)
    pile_top       : Discard               // the discard pile's take-able top card
    pile_rest      : Discard               // everything beneath it (public history)
    meldA[team]    : TeamPile<team>        // the side's meld of aces …
    meldK[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meldQ[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meldJ[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld10[team]   : TeamPile<team>
    meld9[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld8[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld7[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld6[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld5[team]    : TeamPile<team>
    meld4[team]    : TeamPile<team>        // … one team-indexed family per rank
    meld3b[team]   : TeamPile<team>        // the going-out black-three group
    red3[team]     : TeamPile<team>        // laid-out red threes (bonus cards)
  }

  state {
    score[team]  : Integer = 0
    deals_played : Integer = 0
    dealer       : Player  = 0   // seat 0 opens; the deal rotates left
  }

  phase match {

    phase deals repeat until deals_played >= 4 {

      phase hand {
        state {
          opener            : Player  = 0      // dealer's left; leads the hand
          hand_over         : Boolean = false
          turn_done         : Boolean = false
          pile_frozen       : Boolean = false  // wild discard / wild-or-red-3 turn-up
          taking_pile       : Boolean = false  // the open attempt is a pile take
          meld_rank         : Rank?   = none   // the open attempt's rank (none = closed)
          team_melded[team] : Boolean = false
          went_out[team]    : Integer = 0
        }

        phase deal {
          move all cards to deck
          shuffle deck
          deal 11 cards from deck to each hand
          // Red threes dealt are laid out at once and replaced from the stock.
          for each player p: repeat until (number of cards in hand[p] where canasta_is_red3(card)) is 0 {
            move 1 card from hand[p] where canasta_is_red3(card) to red3[team_of(p)]
            draw 1 card from deck to hand[p]
          }
          // Turn up the pile's first card; a wild or red three stacks
          // beneath (freezing the pile) until a start card appears.
          deal 1 cards from deck to pile_top
          repeat until (not canasta_is_wild(top_of(pile_top))) and (not canasta_is_red3(top_of(pile_top))) {
            move all cards from pile_top to pile_rest
            pile_frozen := true
            deal 1 cards from deck to pile_top
          }
          opener := dealer offset_by left
        }

        // --- The turn loop: draw or take, sweep drawn red threes, then the
        // meld window until the turn ends by discard or going out.
        phase play {
          turns t from opener over all players until hand_over {
            turn_done := false

            if deck is empty {
              // No stock: the pile take is forced when the top card matches
              // a standing meld of the side and the pile is not frozen
              // against it; otherwise it may be taken if legal, and a
              // player entitled to draw who does not take ends the hand.
              if canasta_must_take_pile(t) {
                offer to t one of [take_pile]
              } else {
                if canasta_can_take_pile(t) {
                  offer to t one of [take_pile, decline_pile]
                } else {
                  hand_over := true
                  turn_done := true
                }
              }
            } else {
              offer to t one of [draw_stock, take_pile]
            }

            // A drawn red three is laid out and replaced at once; drawing a
            // red three as the stock's last card ends the hand (no meld, no
            // discard).
            repeat until (number of cards in hand[t] where canasta_is_red3(card)) is 0 {
              move 1 card from hand[t] where canasta_is_red3(card) to red3[team_of(t)]
              if deck is empty {
                hand_over := true
                turn_done := true
              } else {
                draw 1 card from deck to hand[t]
              }
            }

            repeat until turn_done {
              if meld_rank is none {
                offer to t one of [start_meld, add_to_meld, meld_black3, end_discard]
              } else {
                offer to t one of [stage_card, close_meld]
              }
              // Going out: every card shed (melded, or the last one
              // discarded) with the attempt closed. The guards allowed it
              // only with a canasta on the side's row.
              if (hand[t] is empty) and (meld_rank is none) {
                went_out[team_of(t)] := 1
                hand_over := true
                turn_done := true
              }
            }
          }
        }

        // --- Hand settlement: melded card points, canasta bonuses (each
        // meld pile scored as an object, by its own composition), red-three
        // bonuses (sign by whether the side melded), the going-out 100;
        // then each player's remaining hand counts against their side.
        phase scoring {
          for each team u: score[u] += canasta_meld_points(u) + canasta_canasta_bonus(u)
                                       + canasta_red3_bonus(u) + 100 * went_out[u]
          for each player p: score[team_of(p)] -= sum of card_points(card) over cards in hand[p]
          deals_played += 1
          dealer := dealer offset_by left
        }
      }
    }
  }

  winner: highest score
}

// --- the draw window ---

move_type draw_stock {
  when: deck is not empty
  effect { draw 1 card from deck to hand[actor] }
}

// Take the whole discard pile: opens a meld attempt on the top card's rank
// with the top card already staged; the REST of the pile joins the hand only
// when the attempt closes (so only the top card can count toward an initial
// meld's minimum — structural, not checked). Guarded by the complete take
// legality: frozen-pile pair justification, unfrozen meld-or-pair, the
// initial minimum, and go-out safety (canasta.py, `canasta_can_take_pile`).
move_type take_pile {
  when: canasta_can_take_pile(actor)
  effect {
    meld_rank := top_of(pile_top).rank
    taking_pile := true
    move all cards from pile_top to stage[actor]
  }
}

// Decline the no-stock pile take: the player is entitled to draw, the stock
// is empty, so the hand ends (offered only beside a legal, unforced take).
move_type decline_pile {
  effect {
    hand_over := true
    turn_done := true
  }
}

// --- the meld window ---

// Announce a new meld of a rank (the eleven-rank parameter domain is the
// declared partial ranking). Legal while the side has no meld of that rank
// and a legal close is reachable from the hand — including the initial-meld
// minimum while the side has not yet melded.
move_type start_meld(rank : Rank) {
  when: canasta_can_start(actor, rank)
  effect { meld_rank := rank }
}

// Stage one card into the open attempt: a natural of the announced rank or a
// wild, and only if a legal close stays reachable (the per-card totality
// guard — a staged position can always close, random play included).
move_type stage_card {
  when: any card in hand[actor] where canasta_stage_ok(actor, card)
  effect {
    move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_stage_ok(actor, card) to stage[actor]
  }
}

// Commit the open attempt to the side's meld pile of its rank. On a pile
// take this is also the moment the rest of the pile flushes into the hand
// (its red threes to the side's row) and the pile unfreezes — a new pile
// starts from the next discard.
move_type close_meld {
  when: canasta_close_ok(actor)
  effect {
    if meld_rank is A { move all cards from stage[actor] to meldA[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is K { move all cards from stage[actor] to meldK[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is Q { move all cards from stage[actor] to meldQ[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is J { move all cards from stage[actor] to meldJ[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "10" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld10[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "9" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld9[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "8" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld8[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "7" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld7[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "6" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld6[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if meld_rank is "5" { move all cards from stage[actor] to meld5[team_of(actor)] }
    else {
      // Structurally meld_rank is "4" here: start_meld's domain and the
      // take guard admit exactly the eleven declared natural ranks.
      move all cards from stage[actor] to meld4[team_of(actor)]
    } } } } } } } } } }
    team_melded[team_of(actor)] := true
    if taking_pile {
      move all cards from pile_rest where canasta_is_red3(card) to red3[team_of(actor)]
      move all cards from pile_rest to hand[actor]
      taking_pile := false
      pile_frozen := false
    }
    meld_rank := none
  }
}

// Lay one card directly onto the side's standing meld of a rank — either
// partner, any turn: the growing half of the shared meld object. A natural
// of the rank always fits; a wild while the pile holds fewer than three.
move_type add_to_meld(rank : Rank) {
  when: any card in hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card)
  effect {
    if rank is A { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meldA[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is K { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meldK[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is Q { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meldQ[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is J { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meldJ[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "10" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld10[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "9" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld9[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "8" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld8[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "7" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld7[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "6" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld6[team_of(actor)] }
    else { if rank is "5" { move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld5[team_of(actor)] }
    else {
      // Structurally rank is "4" here (the declared Rank domain).
      move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_add_ok(actor, rank, card) to meld4[team_of(actor)]
    } } } } } } } } } }
  }
}

// Meld the black threes — only ever as part of going out: the side owns a
// canasta and the hand is exactly the group (3–4 black threes), plus at most
// one card for the final discard. No wilds may join the group.
move_type meld_black3 {
  when: canasta_black3_ok(actor)
  effect {
    move all cards from hand[actor] where canasta_is_black3(card) to meld3b[team_of(actor)]
  }
}

// End the turn with a discard. The previous top retires under the new one; a
// wild discard freezes the pile. Discarding the LAST card is going out and
// was only offered with a canasta on the side's row (`canasta_discard_ok`).
move_type end_discard {
  when: any card in hand[actor] where canasta_discard_ok(actor, card)
  effect {
    move all cards from pile_top to pile_rest
    move chosen one card from hand[actor] where canasta_discard_ok(actor, card) to pile_top
    if canasta_is_wild(top_of(pile_top)) { pile_frozen := true }
    turn_done := true
  }
}

// --- the game's own sentences: card classes, the canasta test, and the
// window guards that need no joint reasoning. The meld-attempt core (joint
// meld legality, take justification, initial minimums, go-out safety under
// composition) stays in cardlang/runtime/canasta.py.

// Jokers and deuces are wild.
function canasta_is_wild(c : Card) = c.rank is Joker or c.rank is "2"

// A red three: a bonus card, laid out and replaced on sight, never melded.
function canasta_is_red3(c : Card) =
  c.rank is "3" and (c.suit is hearts or c.suit is diamonds)

// A black three: a stop card; meldable only as the going-out group.
function canasta_is_black3(c : Card) =
  c.rank is "3" and (c.suit is clubs or c.suit is spades)

// The card points of everything the side melded (canastas included; red
// threes are bonus objects, never meld) — summed over every meld pile, the
// black-three go-out pile included.
function canasta_meld_points(u : Team) =
  (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meldA[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meldK[u])
  + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meldQ[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meldJ[u])
  + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld10[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld9[u])
  + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld8[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld7[u])
  + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld6[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld5[u])
  + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld4[u]) + (sum of card_points(card) over cards in meld3b[u])

// Does the side own a canasta (a seven-card meld)? Scanned over every meld
// pile, the black-three go-out pile included.
function canasta_has_canasta(u : Team) =
  (number of cards in meldA[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meldK[u]) >= 7
  or (number of cards in meldQ[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meldJ[u]) >= 7
  or (number of cards in meld10[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meld9[u]) >= 7
  or (number of cards in meld8[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meld7[u]) >= 7
  or (number of cards in meld6[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meld5[u]) >= 7
  or (number of cards in meld4[u]) >= 7 or (number of cards in meld3b[u]) >= 7

// May `p` end the turn by discarding? Any card may go (`c` is deliberately
// unread — the choice is free); discarding the LAST card is going out,
// legal only once the side has a canasta.
function canasta_discard_ok(p : Player, c : Card) =
  (number of cards in hand[p]) >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))

// May `p` meld their black threes? Only as part of going out: the side has
// a canasta, and the hand is three or four black threes plus at most one
// other card (the final discard).
function canasta_black3_ok(p : Player) =
  canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
  and ((number of cards in hand[p] where canasta_is_black3(card)) is 3
       or (number of cards in hand[p] where canasta_is_black3(card)) is 4)
  and ((number of cards in hand[p]) is (number of cards in hand[p] where canasta_is_black3(card))
       or (number of cards in hand[p]) is (number of cards in hand[p] where canasta_is_black3(card)) + 1)

// May `c` be laid onto the side's standing meld of `r`? A natural of the
// rank always fits; a wild while the pile holds fewer than three wilds.
// Guarded by go-out safety: the add leaves two cards in hand, or the side
// with (or completing) a canasta. One arm per meld family — the zone-family
// flattening's dispatch, exactly as in close_meld / add_to_meld.
function canasta_add_ok(p : Player, r : Rank, c : Card) =
  if r is A then
    meldA[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is A or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meldA[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meldA[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is K then
    meldK[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is K or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meldK[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meldK[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is Q then
    meldQ[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is Q or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meldQ[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meldQ[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is J then
    meldJ[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is J or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meldJ[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meldJ[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "10" then
    meld10[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "10" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld10[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld10[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "9" then
    meld9[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "9" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld9[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld9[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "8" then
    meld8[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "8" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld8[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld8[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "7" then
    meld7[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "7" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld7[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld7[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "6" then
    meld6[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "6" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld6[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld6[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  elif r is "5" then
    meld5[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "5" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld5[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld5[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)
  else
    // Structurally r is "4" here: the declared partial ranking is the Rank
    // parameter domain (threes and the wild ranks are excluded by
    // construction).
    meld4[team_of(p)] is not empty
    and (c.rank is "4" or (canasta_is_wild(c)
         and (number of cards in meld4[team_of(p)] where canasta_is_wild(card)) < 3))
    and ((number of cards in hand[p]) - 1 >= 2 or canasta_has_canasta(team_of(p))
         or (number of cards in meld4[team_of(p)]) + 1 >= 7)

// The red-three bonus: 100 each (800 for all four), positive once the side
// has melded, negative while it has not.
function canasta_red3_bonus(u : Team) =
  if team_melded[u]
  then (if (number of cards in red3[u]) is 4 then 800
        else 100 * (number of cards in red3[u]))
  else 0 - (if (number of cards in red3[u]) is 4 then 800
            else 100 * (number of cards in red3[u]))
